# i18n with literal keys

- Every user-facing string in `apps/web` comes from `@pdf-insight/i18n` through
  `t('literal.key')`, including `aria-label`, `title` and `alt` text. No hard-coded UI strings.
- Keys are string literals at the call site: `t('upload.dropHint')`, never
  `t('error.' + code)` or a template string. `MessageKey` is the union of the catalog keys, so a
  typo is a type error and every use of a key is found by a plain search.
- When the key depends on data, map the value to a literal key in a typed table instead of
  building the key (`errorKeyFor(code)` in `apps/web/src/app/state.ts`, the document type
  labels in `ResultView.tsx`).
- The catalogs are `packages/i18n/src/catalogs/pl.json` (the default locale) and `en.json`, with
  flat dotted keys. Add every key to both files in the same commit: `bun run lint` runs the
  parity check and fails when one catalog has a key the other lacks.
- Placeholders are `{name}` and are filled from `t(key, params)`. Numbers and dates are
  formatted with `Intl` for the active locale, not by hand.
- A missing string falls back to the key itself, so a gap shows on screen. That is a safety
  net, not a substitute for the parity check.
- Code, comments and docs are in English; Polish user-facing text lives only in the `pl`
  catalog.
